ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  With the coming of the spring season, Mugai set out to quench his thirst 
for glory.  He cast a Tornado spell.  Magical tornadoes hit the defenders of 
Ngara.  The Tornado affected no armies in Ngara.  His efforts raised his 
skill in Element Magic.
  The wet spring was followed by early summer.  Mugai tried a Bless spell, 
but botched it.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Mugai's Skeletal Army spell 
backfired and Mugai wound up with his face covered with psycho-kinetic goo.
  In fall, Mugai worked hard on his Necromancy but was frustrated in his 
efforts.
  The fall cooled into early winter.  Mugai practiced his Element Magic 
well, and even consulted an astrologer, but could not improve his skill in 
Element Magic.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Cosmic Herderer Mugai for this year.


  Mugai treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Mugai Treated with Hokuto, 
but Hokuto did not react favorably to his amicable overtures.  It is hoped 
that next year, both Kings will see the wisdom of Treating.
  Mugai treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Mugai treated with his ally 
II Kahn (#6).  Mugai treated with his ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Mugai 
treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Mugai treated with his ally Agesilao (#9).

  Here is the financial report for Mugai's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 10 gold in revenue.  2 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Mugai was left with 59 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Samantha
To: Mugai

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I moved into the Valiant Sea.  I encountered no monster.
  Windy spring blossomed into a fragrant early summer.  I rode into Tabora.  
While adventuring, I encountered no wandering monsters.
  With the coming of the late summer season, I travelled to Ngara.  I 
encountered no monsters.
  During fall, I was instructed in Necromancy by Mugai.  I studied and 
practiced my Necromancy and my skill in Necromancy went up.
  The fall season cooled into the stillness of early winter.  I was 
instructed in the art of Element Magic by Mugai.  I tried to improve my 
Element Magic, but the task was beyond my aptitude.

  Thy humble servant,   Samantha


